id: pm-3g3f8z
title: "Progressive MCP discovery and canonical tool results: reveal the minimum relevant catalog and deliver one unambiguous model-facing output contract"
description: Reduce tool-selection cost and ambiguity at large MCP surface sizes by offering a bounded entry catalog that expands with intent and by standardizing which tool result representation reaches the model. Reuse pm relevance scoring and token-budget primitives through public SDK contracts.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:mcp","area:sdk",progressive-discovery,result-contract,token-efficiency,tool-selection,tools
created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:27.057Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-31T18:27:57.793Z"
deadline: "2027-03-31T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-31T18:27:57.138Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-31T18:27:57.138Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 840
acceptance_criteria: A server advertises a small stable entry catalog and a deterministic expansion mechanism; discovery honors explicit token cost and omission recovery contracts; ranking composes lexical semantic graph permission freshness and usage signals without hiding policy; tool results have one canonical model-facing representation with compatibility adapters isolated; cache hints invalidation and deterministic ordering remain coherent across progressive pages; quality is gated by selection accuracy latency token cost and negative controls at one hundred one thousand and larger tool catalogs; CLI MCP and SDK surfaces derive from one contract
parent: pm-opw1l3
risk: high
confidence: medium
resolution: "Shipped the public SDK discovery engine and negotiated MCP progressive capability with signed cursors, page-correct caching, runtime domain and own-property validation, exact linear budgets, unique measured orientation protocols, compatibility preservation, and lint-safe integration proof."
expected_result: "SDK consumers can build permission-safe progressively disclosed tool catalogs, and agents can rely on unique measured orientation alternatives, live ownership checks, one canonical result representation, page-correct cache semantics, and analyzer-clean tests."
actual_result: "The public SDK provides deterministic permission-safe discovery with HMAC-bound cursors, runtime-validated public filters, prototype-safe tool lookup, page-scoped private cache identities, exact linear token-budget selection, and 10,000-tool scale coverage. Generated guidance and orientation gates enforce live ownership and unique alternatives; all integration assertions are analyzer-safe."
