comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:22:27.057Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: all-status searches for MCP progressive discovery tool catalog scale canonical tool results and result ambiguity found completed cache and stateless owners plus CLI tiering work but no item for the official forward primitive."
  "2026-08-31T12:54:38.703Z","harness:codex","Implementation start: public SDK owns deterministic progressive tool discovery, explicit ranking/budget/omission/cache contracts, and canonical results; MCP and CLI remain adapters. Compatibility is opt-in under a namespaced experimental capability, preserving unnegotiated clients."
  "2026-08-31T13:24:40.554Z","harness:codex","Implementation progress: the public SDK now owns a deterministic discovery contract with six visible signal components, permission filtering, tier/family filters, opaque request-bound cursors, token ceilings, omission recovery, and cache invalidation. Modern opt-in MCP clients receive five entry tools and canonical structured results; compatibility clients retain the full catalog and prior result text."
  "2026-08-31T15:13:29.334Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: linked discovery/MCP/grammar suite passed 24 tests across 3 files. The repository-wide coverage gate passed 8,184 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements (60,524/60,524), branches (45,719/45,719), functions (12,594/12,594), and lines (58,275/58,275). Typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, generated contracts, SDK surface, package boundary/parity, docs/skills, security scan, npm audit, graph composition, record integrity, npx/bunx packed smoke, and a packed npm+Bun isolated lifecycle acceptance all passed. Discovery scale and cursor tests cover 100, 1,000, and 10,000 tools. Standard repository scan 631f1b20-2985-441d-8e88-bc932d167be7 and frozen-diff scan d9fc6148-a705-4c27-8e89-1ba38a270671 found no security findings."
  "2026-08-31T15:27:57.474Z","harness:codex","Final branch evidence: the complete quality:static pipeline passed after closure, including defect-evidence classification, repository assurance negative controls, token/context calibration, generated surfaces, package and SDK parity, MCP deprecation inventory, transport floor, graph composition, and record integrity. Security secret scan and dependency audit also passed with 0 vulnerabilities across all severities."
  "2026-08-31T16:11:23.688Z","harness:codex","Review round 1 remediation: accepted both Greptile findings. Detached task failures now retain negotiated canonical structured errors. Discovery cursors now carry an HMAC integrity tag under the private process cache, so modifying even an in-range offset fails closed; malformed, unsigned, stale, and out-of-range negative controls are covered. DeepScan's two nullable-access findings were removed with runtime-checked tool parsing. The Claude compatibility smoke and docs now lock all 32 tools including pm_discover. The live complexity provider reports zero violations, focused suites/typecheck/plugin smoke pass, and the full repository suite passes 8,185 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-31T17:25:34.245Z","harness:codex","Review round 2 evidence: CodeRabbit findings were verified against the current source. Runtime-invalid tier/family inputs now fail closed; cache keys are page-scoped across fingerprint, limit, offset, and budget while cursor binding remains request-scoped; the canonical README path is one measured orientation call; optional guide setup is separated from read-only pre-mutation checks; and budget selection serializes each schema-bearing row once while retaining exact envelope accounting. Linked suites passed 28 and 34 tests. The full repository gate passed 8,188 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements 60,555/60,555, branches 45,740/45,740, functions 12,602/12,602, and lines 58,304/58,304. The live and aggregate static gates report zero complexity/docstring/duplication/boundary violations; secret scan and dependency audit are clean."
  "2026-08-31T18:09:23.548Z","harness:codex","Review round 3 evidence: accepted four CodeRabbit edge cases. The orientation token gate now rejects duplicate protocol task IDs; generated guidance includes live in-progress ownership checks before item mutation; SDK discovery treats Object.prototype names as unregistered help-backed candidates; and runtime tier validation rejects internal plus malformed values. Linked suites pass 29, 35, and 33 tests. Full coverage passes 8,189 tests across 593 files at exact 100% statements 60,558/60,558, branches 45,741/45,741, functions 12,603/12,603, and lines 58,307/58,307. Full static quality, live provider, secret scan, and dependency audit pass."
  "2026-08-31T18:27:56.027Z","harness:codex","Release preflight remediation: CodeFactor annotation 99591861337 identified an unsafe optional-chain cast/index assertion in mcp-progressive-discovery.integration.spec.ts. The assertion now matches the complete optional content array with a stringContaining matcher, eliminating the possible undefined dereference. Focused integration test and file-scoped ESLint pass. Production source is unchanged from the 8,189-test exact 100/100/100/100 and full static run."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-31T15:07:54.738Z","harness:codex",Progressive discovery must bind cursors to the authorization-filtered ranked request and refuse budgets that cannot advance; a non-advancing cursor is worse than an explicit recoverable minimum-budget error.
  "2026-08-31T17:25:34.767Z","harness:codex","Cursor authorization identity and response cache identity are different contracts: keep the signed request fingerprint stable across adjustable page size/budget, but key cached responses by fingerprint plus offset, limit, and budget. Exact token budgeting can remain linear by pre-serializing rows once and measuring a constant-size empty-tools envelope."
  "2026-08-31T18:09:24.045Z","harness:codex","Runtime SDK inputs must validate the public domain rather than a broader internal lookup table, and string-keyed public registries must use own-property checks because prototype names are valid untrusted input. Measured protocol alternatives also need unique identities, not only a minimum row count."
